From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DolphinSlicer <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:28:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] BridgeDetector: order tied bridge directions the same on
 all platforms

std::sort is not stable and each standard library orders equal elements differently.
Bridge direction candidates sorted by coverage often tie (0 and 90 degrees over a square
overhang), and the first candidate wins, so the bridge direction (and the G-code) differed
between Linux, macOS and Windows builds.

Add PortableSort.hpp, an exact port of libstdc++'s std::sort introsort (verified to order
ties identically to libstdc++ 15, including the heap-sort fallback), and use it here.
Linux results are unchanged; other platforms now match Linux.
Upstreamable: yes.
---
